WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.200
An emergency is an unexpected and serious situation where someone needs help right away.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:12.100
A medical emergency is a specific kind of danger where a person is so sick or badly

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:16.719
hurt that they need a doctor or ambulance immediately to save their life or prevent

00:00:16.719 --> 00:00:18.440
serious harm.

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:24.000
Whatever the situation, if you believe it is necessary to call 911, then go ahead and

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.480
make that call.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:29.280
If it turns out to be a false alarm, that is perfectly okay.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:35.759
It is always better to be cautious and call early than to wait until it might be too late.

00:00:35.759 --> 00:00:40.840
When you call 911, the dispatcher will ask you several questions, which we will go over

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.259
shortly.

00:00:42.259 --> 00:00:47.200
To make the process easier, put your phone on speaker immediately.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:52.419
This also allows you to follow the dispatcher's instructions and provide care while still

00:00:52.419 --> 00:00:56.000
being able to listen and talk to them.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.400
Dispatchers are trained to coach you through CPR and other life-saving steps over the phone.

